    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Pv7S1jGET3Yr"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Import Libraries**\n",
        "\n",
        "Before building an ANN model, we need:\n",
        "\n",
        "Visualization -- matplotlib, seaborn\n",
        "\n",
        "Deep Learning -- TensorFlow/Keras\n",
        "\n",
        "Preprocessing & evaluation -- scikit-learn\n",
        "\n",
        "These libraries help in:\n",
        "\n",
        "Preparing data\n",
        "\n",
        "Building model\n",
        "\n",
        "Evaluating performance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "15l_gW4rSr3R"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "from tensorflow import keras\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras import layers\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras.utils import to_categorical\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras.callbacks import EarlyStopping\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, LabelEncoder\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix, mean_squared_error\n",
        "\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hp268bCOUe87"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 1: Load Dataset**\n",
        "\n",
        "We load the Iris dataset which contains:\n",
        "\n",
        "150 samples\n",
        "4 input features\n",
        "3 output classes\n",
        "\n",
        "This dataset is ideal because:\n",
        "\n",
        "Small and clean\n",
        "Perfect for ANN demonstration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "5SJHzQOAUdWL",
        "outputId": "4992160f-537d-4b5e-9331-b26ff464e2eb"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "(150, 4) (150,)\n",
            "   sepal length (cm)  sepal width (cm)  petal length (cm)  petal width (cm)\n",
            "0                5.1               3.5                1.4               0.2\n",
            "1                4.9               3.0                1.4               0.2\n",
            "2                4.7               3.2                1.3               0.2\n",
            "3                4.6               3.1                1.5               0.2\n",
            "4                5.0               3.6                1.4               0.2\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "iris = load_iris()\n",
        "\n",
        "X = pd.DataFrame(iris.data, columns=iris.feature_names)\n",
        "y = pd.Series(iris.target)\n",
        "\n",
        "target_names = iris.target_names\n",
        "\n",
        "print(X.shape, y.shape)\n",
        "print(X.head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ASjxCD-rVbhN"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 2: Encoding Target**\n",
        "\n",
        "Neural networks require numerical input:\n",
        "\n",
        "Labels must be encoded\n",
        "\n",
        "Steps:\n",
        "\n",
        "Label Encoding  -- convert labels to numbers\n",
        "\n",
        "One-hot Encoding   -- required for multi-class classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gqdLH6qpVTPH"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "label_encoder = LabelEncoder()\n",
        "y_encoded = label_encoder.fit_transform(y)\n",
        "\n",
        "num_classes = len(np.unique(y_encoded))\n",
        "y_one_hot = to_categorical(y_encoded)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RBRfJaIvV71x"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 3: Train-Test Split**\n",
        "\n",
        "We split data into:\n",
        "\n",
        "Training set (80%) -- learn patterns\n",
        "\n",
        "Testing set (20%) -- evaluate performance\n",
        "\n",
        "Stratified sampling ensures:\n",
        "\n",
        "Equal class distribution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OJSYotL0WNHW"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train_oh, y_test_oh = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y_one_hot, test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=y_encoded)\n",
        "\n",
        "_, _, _, y_test_original = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y_encoded, test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=y_encoded)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2YL4flRnWv7z"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 4: Feature Scaling**\n",
        "\n",
        "ANN is sensitive to feature scale.\n",
        "\n",
        "Why scaling is important:\n",
        "\n",
        "Faster convergence\n",
        "\n",
        "Prevents dominance of large values\n",
        "\n",
        "Improves accuracy\n",
        "\n",
        "We use **StandardScaler**:\n",
        "\n",
        "Mean = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "Std = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "V3Mk02xCXC0d"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IrDDPWiTXHIz"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 5: Build ANN Model (Classification)**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Model structure:**\n",
        "\n",
        "Input layer -- 4 neurons\n",
        "\n",
        "Hidden layer -- learns patterns\n",
        "\n",
        "Output layer -- 3 classes\n",
        "\n",
        "Activation:\n",
        "\n",
        "ReLU -- hidden layer\n",
        "\n",
        "Softmax -- output layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "n7I5vyYtXXXg"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "    keras.Input(shape=(4,)),\n",
        "    layers.Dense(10, activation='relu'),\n",
        "    layers.Dense(3, activation='softmax')\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "g64ZijuNXmPP"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 6: Compile Model**\n",
        "\n",
        "We define:\n",
        "\n",
        "Optimizer -- Adam (fast & efficient)\n",
        "\n",
        "Loss -- categorical_crossentropy\n",
        "\n",
        "Metric -- accuracy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "euHr9VZfXs5l"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model.compile(optimizer='adam',\n",
        "              loss='categorical_crossentropy',\n",
        "              metrics=['accuracy'])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "uNWj9b03Xxhb"
      },
      "source": [
        "**PART 7: Train Model**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Training process:**\n",
        "\n",
        "Epochs -- number of learning cycles\n",
        "\n",
        "Batch size -- samples per update\n",
        "\n",
        "Validation -- check overfitting"
      ]
    },
